---

---

<main>
  <section id="splash-page">
    <!-- this is purely decorative content, remove it from a11y tree -->
    <div class="solar-system-container" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="solar-system">
        <div class="sun"></div>
        <div class="planets">
          <div></div>
          <div></div>
          <div></div>
          <div class="mars"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="hero">
    <h1 id="about">
      I'm JE<span>RED MARS</span>HALL. <br /> I make things for the Web.
    </h1>
    <p>Performant, delightful, accessible things.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="info">
    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a Frontend Software Engineer living in Austin, TX. I've been
      developing for the web for 15+ years and I believe that websites should be
      fast and easy to use, no matter <b>who you are</b>, <b>where you live</b>,
      or <b>what device you own</b>. I enjoy designing and developing websites
      and web apps. Taking in client/product feedback, researching new tools,
      working out the little puzzles that coding provides. Above all, I like to
      create fun, easily understandable experiences for users.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="info">
    <h2>Why the focus on Accessibility?</h2>
    <p>
      Accessible websites are better websites. But in terms of FE development,
      the industry still misses the mark <a
        href="https://webaim.org/projects/million/#errors"
        >pretty consistently</a
      >. We should try to be an exception to that trend and ensure our sites are
      usable for all. I love to browse using keyboard navigation, so its a
      moment of delight for me when a website supports that. I don't have an
      eyesight or motor impairment, but if I can still navigate using the
      keyboard, it improves my experience. Ensuring an interface is usable for a
      specific browsing method doesn't just improve the UX for one group of
      people, it improves it for everyone.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="info">
    <h2>Why the focus on performance?</h2>
    <p>
      Its not a secret that the web is pretty bloated. Unnecessary scripts and
      large photos slow websites down and cause users money when they have to
      download all that information. Where possible, be intentional with the
      data you send to the user. Not every user lives in the <a
        href="https://www.smashingmagazine.com/2017/03/world-wide-web-not-wealthy-western-web-part-1/"
        >Wealthy Western Web</a
      > (that link is old by internet standards, but has always stuck in my head).
      At the end of the day, its all about providing a good experience to users.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

<style>
  @keyframes spin {
    0% {
      transform: rotateZ(0deg);
    }
    100% {
      transform: rotateZ(-360deg);
    }
  }

  main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacer-2);
  }

  #splash-page {
    /* margin-top: var(--spacer-3); */
    @media screen and (min-width: 768px) {
      margin-top: 0;
      width: 100vw;
      /* height: 100vh; */
      height: calc(100vh - var(--spacer-2) * 2 - var(--spacer));
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
  }

  #splash-page ~ section {
    max-inline-size: 80ch;
    margin: 0 auto var(--spacer-2);
    padding-inline: var(--spacer);
  }
  #hero {
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.75;
    text-wrap: pretty;
    margin: var(--spacer-3) 0 var(--spacer);
    font-family:
      ui-monospace, "Cascadia Code", "Source Code Pro", Menlo, Consolas,
      "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;

    p {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }
  }
  h1 {
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: pretty;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2vw + 1rem, 3rem);
    padding: var(--spacer-2) 0 0;
    margin-block-end: var(--spacer-2);
    background-color: var(--background);
    span {
      color: var(--accent);
    }
  }

  h2 {
    margin-block-end: var(--spacer);
  }

  p {
    /* font-size: 1.2rem; */
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .solar-system-container {
    inline-size: 100%;
    height: fit-content;
    position: relative;
    margin-block-end: var(--spacer-2);
  }
  .solar-system {
    position: relative;
    perspective: 1000px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    & > * {
      grid-area: 1/1;
    }
  }
  .sun {
    width: 3vw;
    height: 3vw;
    background-color: var(--foreground);
    /* background-color: yellow; */
    border-radius: 100%;
  }
  /* planets */
  .planets {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    place-items: center;

    transform: rotateX(80deg) rotateY(-10deg);
    transform-style: preserve-3d;

    & > * {
      grid-area: 1/1;
    }

    .sun {
      background-color: var(--foreground);
    }

    div {
      --orbitSize: 70vw;
      background-color: transparent;
      border-radius: 100%;
      border: 2px solid var(--foreground);
      border: clamp(4px, 0.5vw, 0.5vw) solid var(--foreground);

      @supports not (max-inline-size: calc(40rem * (sibling-index() / 4))) {
        &:nth-child(1) {
          inline-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (1 / 4));
          block-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (1 / 4));

          /* max-inline-size: calc(40rem * (1 / 4));
          max-block-size: calc(40rem * (1 / 4)); */
        }
        &:nth-child(2) {
          inline-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (2 / 4));
          block-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (2 / 4));

          /* max-inline-size: calc(40rem * (2 / 4));
          max-block-size: calc(40rem * (2 / 4)); */
        }
        &:nth-child(3) {
          inline-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (3 / 4));
          block-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (3 / 4));

          /* max-inline-size: calc(40rem * (3 / 4));
          max-block-size: calc(40rem * (3 / 4)); */
        }
        &:nth-child(4) {
          inline-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (4 / 4));
          block-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (4 / 4));

          /* max-inline-size: calc(40rem * (4 / 4));
          max-block-size: calc(40rem * (4 / 4)); */
        }
      }

      /* progressively enhance with sibling-index stuff */
      @supports (max-inline-size: calc(40rem * (sibling-index() / 4))) {
        inline-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (sibling-index() / 4));
        block-size: calc(var(--orbitSize) * (sibling-index() / 4));

        max-inline-size: calc(100vw * (sibling-index() / 4));
        max-block-size: calc(100vw * (sibling-index() / 4));

        /* max-inline-size: calc(40rem * (sibling-index() / 4)); */
        /* max-block-size: calc(40rem * (sibling-index() / 4)); */
      }
    }

    .mars {
      position: relative;
      transform-style: preserve-3d;
      transform: rotateZ(65deg);

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
        animation: spin 20s linear infinite;
      }

      &:before,
      &:after {
        content: "";
        display: block;
        width: 1.5vw;
        height: 1.5vw;
        border-radius: 100%;
        background-color: var(--accent);
        position: absolute;
        right: 0;
        top: calc(50% + 2px);
      }
      &:before {
        transform: translate(50%, -50%) rotateX(90deg);
      }
      &:after {
        transform: translate(50%, -50%) rotateX(90deg) rotateY(90deg);
      }
    }
  }
</style>
